 α′-corrected nonperturbative potential supply a saddle approaching the logarithmically extended TCC duration bound?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0052"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bfec1c0ac07fd397043af6a2e551f102680aa5eb9478e93c6b37aaab5dddd4e7","title":"How does this extension's inflationary H bound compare with TCC constraints in k-inflation, and what additional conditions arise from distance and Lyth bounds?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0061"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bf58ea8327a85e67aa6c70c5dcaacb5880b6c6efcf568846f2101db855d68636","title":"Assuming the Finite Action Principle, which early-universe, black-hole and wormhole geometries have finite ultraviolet action in Hořava–Lifshitz gravity, and can this provide a selection mechanism for cosmological initial conditions and singularity avoidance?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bff5f38896802d1c22a015771b36398fd9925228457e3cf6424900f472bc9bc9","title":"Can production of descending tower states alter quintessence materially, beyond merely invalidating their integration out?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bfeda7377f0cd2c1dfcfab590c29787441f907c2c20f55093d4b6f5d9828af5a","title":"How do general P¹-bundles and degenerating P¹-fibrations enlarge F-theory base geometries, and how do base transitions, rational sections and fiber monodromy modify heterotic/F-theory duality?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bf4f96dbac6614961d5ed89ae5b3feb7664a221f78bb1ec716063aaeff1b79b5","title":"The local example compares valuations for an elliptic curve with potential good reduction and its good-reduction